;;; A value `(eq Ann Bob)` inside a fact is stored —
;;; regression `eq-value-fact`.
;;;
;;; ── What this program is ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
;;;
;;; Two guests and what Ann says, `(says Ann (eq Ann Bob))`. No candidate.
;;;
;;; ── The answer, by hand ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
;;;
;;; `eq` is the relation of equality, computed and never stored (Q-M1e2.26), so
;;; `(eq …)` is no value (Q-M1f.124): refused at the parse, at `eq`, on every
;;; command, as `(says Ann (neq Ann Bob))` is.
;;;
;;; ── What the engine answered ──────────────────────────────────────────────
;;;
;;; At `52e05fc1`, release: the program loads and stores `(says Ann (eq Ann Bob))`, an
;;; equality nothing computes, and the goal answers `?c = (eq Ann Bob)`, exit 0 on
;;; every command.
;;; The engine now refuses it at the parse, on every command.
;;;

(relation paid Guest :why "{?3} has paid")
(is-a Ann Guest) (is-a Bob Guest)
(relation says Guest Claim :why "{?3} says {?4}")
(says Ann (eq Ann Bob))
(solve :hypothesis-relations ())
(query :goal (says ?g ?c))
